      "body": "## Motivation\n\nInkling doesn't start on SM120 GPUs (RTX 50 series, RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell). The server dies while capturing decode CUDA graphs:\n\n```\nFile \".../sglang/kernels/ops/moe/inkling_moe.py\", line 998, in grouped_gemm_triton\n    _grouped_gemm_kernel[grid](\ntriton.runtime.errors.OutOfResources: out of resource: shared memory, Required: 110592, Hardware limit: 101376.\n```\n\nThe small-M grouped GEMM config (used for decode, up to 6144 routed tokens) runs with `num_stages=4`. With 16x128x128 bf16 tiles, Triton keeps 3 stage buffers in shared memory: 3 x 36,864 B = 110,592 B. SM120 only allows 101,376 B per block.\n\nThis was already fixed for SM121 (GB10 / DGX Spark) in [#33108](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/33108). SM121 has the same 99 KB limit, but that fix only checks `is_sm121()`, so SM120 still gets 4 stages.\n\nThis affects the NVFP4 checkpoint too, not just BF16. NVFP4 experts use FP4 kernels, but `Inkling-Small-NVFP4` leaves layer 2's experts unquantized (`model.llm.layers.2.mlp.experts` is in `exclude_modules`). Those BF16 experts go through `grouped_gemm_triton`, so the NVFP4 model crashes on SM120 as well.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `inkling_moe.py`: use `num_stages=3` on SM120 as well (`is_sm120() or is_sm121()`). That needs 2 x 36,864 B = 73,728 B, which fits. Other GPUs are unchanged.\n- `test_moe_preprocess.py`: also register the test on the `1-gpu-small` (RTX 5090) runner, the same way `test_convrot_int8.py` does. This test already covers the small-M config, but it only ran on H100, which is why this slipped through.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nOnly the pipeline depth changes. The math is the same, so outputs are identical (same as #33108).\n\nTested on an RTX 5090:\n\n- `test_moe_preprocess.py`: 3 failed / 14 passed before the fix (`test_grouped_gemm_small_config_matches[1|16|64]`, all `OutOfResources`), 17 passed after.\n- I also ran the whole `base-b-kernel-unit-test-1-gpu-small` suite with this change, and nothing else was affected.\n- End to end: the real checkpoint (171 GB) doesn't fit on one card, so I shrank Inkling-Small's config to 3 layers (2 dense + 1 MoE, matching the real model's first layers, 32 experts) and launched it with `--load-format dummy --disable-prefill-cuda-graph`. Before: the server dies in `capture_decode_graph` with the error above. After: it starts and serves `/v1/chat/completions`.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A. This config couldn't launch on SM120 before, and H100/B200 are untouched.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\ncc @yvbbrjdr (author of #33108) @hnyls2002\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39469859339](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39469859339)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39469859281](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39469859281)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39469859697](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39469859697)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
